{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he rolled</b> — twice here, and the other: \"my glory shall rejoice\" (Psalms 57:9). For when he saw her, the Holy Spirit rested upon him, and this is \"my glory shall rejoice,\" as written: \"Awake, my glory\" (Psalms 57:9). Another interpretation: When will \"my glory shall rejoice\" be fulfilled? When \"he rolled the stone\" is fulfilled — when the evil inclination, which is likened to a stone, is removed."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:20.863161233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}